        "original_id": "de60331a-1803-5c76-8bb5-e39ab4c3de18",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Rawlins Park, Foggy Bottom, Washington, D.C.\n- People: General John A. Rawlins\n- Monuments: statue of General John A. Rawlins\n- Topics: place names, relocation history\n\nFacts:\n- The statue of General John A. Rawlins is a focal point of Rawlins Park, a small public park in the Foggy Bottom neighborhood of Washington, D.C.\n- The statue of General John A. Rawlins was installed in 1874.\n- The statue of General John A. Rawlins was relocated several times between 1880 and 1931.\n- Foggy Bottom is thought to have received its name from its riverside location, which made the area susceptible to fog and industrial smoke.",
